    "created_at": "2022-03-25T19:42:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-25T19:42:01Z",
    "body": "Hey Mélanie 👋\r\n\r\nThank you for the hard work you've been putting into translating the docs in French.\r\nCrowdin is a bit of a mystery to me, only having used it for this project. From how it seems, changes seem to cause cascading invalidations, but the data isn't lost! Every month or two, I force Crowdin to \"Pre-translate via TM\", which rescans the project and applies translations from our \"Translation Memory\", which tends to fix all the invalidations.\r\nJust now, I triggered a \"Pre-translate\" and the French translations went from 55% to 83%\r\n\r\nI'm likely not doing it frequently enough. Perhaps there's a way we can automate it via a GitHub Action.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
