    "updated_at": "2022-03-25T21:30:44Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the quick answer!\r\n\r\nI didn’t know about «Pre-translate via TM», that’s really nice! But yeah, the problem is that between the time where strings have been invalidated and the time you apply «Pre-translate via TM», I still have to either ignore strings already translated in the past (it doesn’t seem possible to filter them this way), or to translate them anyway with the Translation Memory but it’s still a lot of strings to go through.\r\n\r\nMaybe Crowdin itself can be configured in a way that either invalidates strings less aggressively, or to trigger pre-translate every time.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
